[gd_scene load_steps=4 format=3 uid="uid://unitdirshadowsplits"]

; A close-up shadow under the DirectionalLight3D's default four splits, and nothing else: the sun
; leaves `directional_shadow_mode` and its split offsets at Godot's defaults. The bars are 0.04 wide,
; under one texel of a single map over the 100-unit shadow range and about three texels of the
; first split's map, so the stripes stay crisp only while the near split draws. Every other shadow
; golden casts from a body many texels wide, which one map resolves too, so a regression to one map
; or a wrong split selection is invisible there.

